{{Quote|We're being sent to my mother's on Talivar.|Flix, on his and Orka's plans to escape the First Order|audio=Talivar-NoEscapePart1.flac|<ref name="No Escape" />}}
'''Flix's mother's home'''<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=star-wars-resistance/no-escape-part-1-episode-gallery|text="No Escape: Part 1" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Episode Gallery slide 6}}</ref> was located on the celestial body [[Talivar]].<ref name="No Escape" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="34 ABY">{{ResistanceDate|1|20}}</ref> business partners [[Flix]] and [[Orka]] intended to have themselves,<ref name="No Escape" /> their pet<ref name="Bitey">{{Databank|bitey|Bitey}}</ref> [[gorg]] [[Bitey]], and the [[DUM-series pit droid|pit droid]] [[G-LN]] shipped from their [[Office of Acquisitions|business]] aboard the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]] ''[[Colossus]]'' to [[Flix's flock|Flix's]] [[Flix's mother|mother's]] home through the [[First Order delivery service]]. However, the [[Mission to contact the Resistance|submerging]] of the ''Colossus'' into<ref name="No Escape" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="Number">{{InsiderCite|190|Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited}}</ref> [[Castilon]]'s [[Water|oceans]] halted that plan.<ref name="No Escape" />

==Behind the scenes==
Flix's mother's home was first mentioned in "[[No Escape: Part 1]],"<ref name="No Escape" /> the twentieth episode of [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|season one]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'',<ref name="Number" /> which aired [[March 10]], [[2019]].<ref name="Disney release">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> The home was identified in the corresponding episode guide.<ref name="Episode Guide" />

